# Committed, non-secret production defaults.
#
# Read this before adding anything here.
#
# Next.js loads this file for production builds AND in the production runtime,
# and a value present here can win over the one configured in Vercel. That makes
# it the wrong place for a placeholder.
#
# This file used to carry placeholder database, NextAuth, Google OAuth and
# Nutrient credentials, added to avoid "Invalid URL" errors during builds. A
# placeholder connection string here can be read in preference to the real Neon
# URL configured in Vercel, which is reason enough not to keep one.
#
# They were also unnecessary: lib/prisma.ts builds its client lazily through a
# Proxy, so nothing connects to a database during the build.
#
# What these placeholders did NOT cause is the production outage that is easy to
# blame on them. Every query failing against 127.0.0.1:5432 was a separate bug —
# the Prisma adapter was handed a `pg.Pool` it could not recognise under pnpm and
# died at protocol startup, reporting a host that was never involved. That is
# explained at length in lib/prisma.ts. Both faults pointed at localhost, which
# is precisely why they were mistaken for one.
#
# Rule: only add a value here if it is not a secret AND it is correct in
# production. Anything else belongs in Vercel's environment settings alone.

# Nutrient Viewer CDN version. Not a secret, and this is the real value, so it is
# safe for it to win. Loaded by app/layout.tsx from
# https://cdn.cloud.pspdfkit.com/pspdfkit-web@<version>/nutrient-viewer.js
NUTRIENT_VIEWER_VERSION="1.20.0"
